## 4. Inventory Operations Review

### Product CRUD

| Operation | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Create product | ✅ | Serializable transaction; creates Product + Inventory + opening transaction + activity |
| Update product | ✅ | Updates product fields + recalculates stock status with new minimumStock |
| Delete (no history) | ✅ | Hard delete with cascaded activity cleanup |
| Delete (with history) | ✅ | Soft delete (archive: `active = false`) preserving transaction history |
| Duplicate SKU handling | ✅ | Returns 409 `SKU_ALREADY_EXISTS` via P2002 catch |
| Category validation | ✅ | `assertOwnedCategory()` verifies category belongs to user |

### Stock Operations

| Operation | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Stock In (receive) | ✅ | Serializable TX; calculates weighted average cost; updates inventory + creates transaction + activity |
| Stock Out (sell) | ✅ | Serializable TX; guarded decrement (`quantity >= requested`); prevents overselling |
| Insufficient stock | ✅ | Returns 409 `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` with available quantity |
| Quantity overflow | ✅ | `DATABASE_QUANTITY_MAX` (2^31-1) enforced at validation and calculation layers |
| Zero quantity rejection | ✅ | Zod schema requires `positive()` |
| Negative quantity rejection | ✅ | Zod schema requires `positive()` |
| Decimal quantity rejection | ✅ | Zod schema requires `int()` |
| Transaction atomicity | ✅ | Serializable isolation level with 3 retry attempts for P2034 |
| Race condition protection | ✅ | `updateMany` with `quantity >= requested` check + serializable isolation |

