### Error Response Structure
All endpoints follow consistent structure:
```json
{ "success": false, "error": { "code": "...", "message": "..." } }
{ "success": true, "message": "...", "data": {...} }
```

### HTTP Status Codes
- `200` — Success
- `201` — Created (products, stock transactions, categories, etc.)
- `202` — Accepted (forgot password, resend verification)
- `400` — Bad request (invalid tokens)
- `401` — Unauthorized
- `403` — Forbidden (email not verified, account unavailable, invalid origin)
- `409` — Conflict (duplicate SKU, insufficient stock, already registered)
- `413` — Payload too large
- `415` — Unsupported media type
- `422` — Validation error (Zod failures, quantity limit exceeded)
- `429` — Rate limited
- `500` — Internal error (with sanitized error details)

